From 17ace3812b7385f00c31cfe9e54d50758108c9b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: webby <webby@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:35:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Windows port: use WebCore's GStreamer media backend

Replaces Media Foundation with the GStreamer backend of the GTK and WPE
ports, which brings Media Source Extensions and Web Audio.

Build: OptionsWin.cmake includes the GStreamer option and check modules and
finds GLib and GStreamer through vcpkg's pkgconf; WTF builds the GLib smart
pointer helpers; WebCore includes platform/GStreamer.cmake. USE(GLIB) stays
off, so the port keeps its Windows run loop, file system and IPC: the wtf/glib
headers the GStreamer code needs accept USE(GSTREAMER) instead.

Port work in the GStreamer code:
- Bus messages reach the RunLoop of the thread that asked for them through
  the bus's sync-message signal, since no GLib main loop runs.
- fnmatch(), /proc/self/cmdline and /var/tmp have Windows equivalents.
- The fallback video sink converts to sRGB BGRx on the GPU (d3d11convert)
  before the frame is downloaded; videoconvert manages 10 frames a second at
  1080p.
- A frame is converted to an image once, not once for every tile painted,
  and frames already in the paint format skip the conversion pipeline.
- When the page is composited the frames go to a WCPlatformLayerImage, which
  the compositor shows as a texture; otherwise they are painted.
- AudioBus loads the HRTF impulse responses from WebKit.resources\audio.

Also fixes code that had not been compiled on Windows before: a dllexport
member of a dllexport class, ssize_t, an atomic_flag initializer, and includes
and calls that were only valid with coordinated graphics or the GLib run loop.
